Subject: pooled embeddings: one sequence per ubatch in attention KV caches

When a batch contains pooled-embedding sequences of unequal length, the
unified/iSWA attention caches split it with split_equal(), which can spread
a sequence across multiple ubatches. Pooling runs per ubatch and the last
ubatch's result overwrites the previous ones, so the returned "mean"
embedding only covers the trailing tokens of the longest sequence(s).

Repro (server, gemma4, --embeddings --pooling mean, -np 2): embedding a
10-token and a 13-token text in one request returns, for the longer text,
exactly mean(tokens[10:13]) instead of mean(tokens[0:13]).

Fix: honor the embd_all flag (as llama_memory_hybrid and the recurrent
cache already do) by using split_seq(), which keeps each sequence whole
within a ubatch.


Note: the llama-kv-cache.cpp (unified cache) half of this fix was
absorbed into the SEBK4C/llamafile fork's llama.cpp overlay at the
0.10.7 bump; only the iSWA-cache half remains here.
diff --git a/src/llama-kv-cache-iswa.cpp b/src/llama-kv-cache-iswa.cpp
index 26e2cb4..f039483 100644
--- a/src/llama-kv-cache-iswa.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-kv-cache-iswa.cpp
@@ -124,7 +124,42 @@ std::map<ggml_backend_buffer_type_t, size_t> llama_kv_cache_iswa::memory_breakdo
 }
 
 llama_memory_context_ptr llama_kv_cache_iswa::init_batch(llama_batch_allocr & balloc, uint32_t n_ubatch, bool embd_all) {
-    GGML_UNUSED(embd_all);
+    // if all tokens are output (pooled embeddings), split by sequence so that a
+    // sequence never spans multiple ubatches — otherwise the pooled embedding
+    // only covers the tokens of its final ubatch
+    if (embd_all) {
+        balloc.split_reset();
+
+        std::vector<llama_ubatch> ubatches;
+        while (true) {
+            auto ubatch = balloc.split_seq(n_ubatch);
+
+            if (ubatch.n_tokens == 0) {
+                break;
+            }
+
+            ubatches.push_back(std::move(ubatch)); // NOLINT
+        }
+
+        if (balloc.get_n_used() < balloc.get_n_tokens()) {
+            return std::make_unique<llama_kv_cache_iswa_context>(LLAMA_MEMORY_STATUS_FAILED_PREPARE);
+        }
+
+        auto sinfos_base = kv_base->prepare(ubatches);
+        if (sinfos_base.empty()) {
+            return std::make_unique<llama_kv_cache_iswa_context>(LLAMA_MEMORY_STATUS_FAILED_PREPARE);
+        }
+
+        auto sinfos_swa = kv_swa->prepare(ubatches);
+        if (sinfos_swa.empty()) {
+            return std::make_unique<llama_kv_cache_iswa_context>(LLAMA_MEMORY_STATUS_FAILED_PREPARE);
+        }
+
+        assert(sinfos_base.size() == sinfos_swa.size());
+
+        return std::make_unique<llama_kv_cache_iswa_context>(
+                this, std::move(sinfos_base), std::move(sinfos_swa), std::move(ubatches));
+    }
 
